---
/**
 * Colophon: what the site is set in, what it is made of, who made it. A
 * standalone page rather than a hub section: one narrow measure, a small
 * object of its own, no rails.
 */

import { place } from "../data/about";
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
---

<Shell
	title="Colophon — Conor Scheidt"
	description="What this site is set in, and what it is made of."
	scrollable
>
	<div class="colo">
		<header class="colo-head">
			<a class="colo-back" href="/">← crs.so</a>
			<canvas class="colo-mark" data-colophon-mark aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
			<h1>Colophon</h1>
		</header>

		<div class="colo-body">
			<p>
				Set in <b>Fraunces</b> — optical size 144 for display, where the letterforms are drawn
				thin and wide — with <b>Spectral</b> at 300 for reading, and <b>JetBrains Mono</b> reserved
				for anything that has to mean exactly one character. Warm black on warm paper.
				Night is the same two inks exchanged, which is why it inverts in a single frame
				and never fades.
			</p>

			<p>
				The object between the menu and the page is <b>4,600 points</b>, positioned entirely in
				a vertex shader — one draw call, no compute pass, no vertex buffer, eighty bytes
				of uniform. A trefoil knot on the index; the edges of an icosahedron under
				Projects; a loxodrome under Writing; three Borromean rings under About. Changing
				section interpolates between two parametrisations rather than swapping models.
				Machines without WebGPU get the same mathematics on a canvas, at a lower count.
			</p>

			<p>
				Built with <b>Astro</b> and TypeScript, drawn with <b>d3</b>, typeset with <b>KaTeX</b>.
				The C and C++ in the essays are compiled in the page by <b>clang</b> and <b>lld</b>,
				carried in as WebAssembly — eighteen megabytes, fetched once and kept — after
				<a href="https://github.com/binji/wasm-clang" rel="noopener">binji&rsquo;s wasm-clang</a>.
				When one of those programs reads standard input it genuinely blocks, on a
				<code>SharedArrayBuffer</code>, until you answer.
			</p>

			<p>
				Static files on Cloudflare. No trackers, no third-party fonts, and no cookie notice
				because there are no cookies. Source at <a href="https://git.crs.so" rel="me">git.crs.so</a>.
			</p>

			<p class="colo-sign">
				Written and set by hand in {place.city}.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Shell>

<script>
	import "../colophon";
</script>
